<html>
<title>Zoom Level and Full Screen Mode</title>
<body>

<h1>Zoom Level and Full Screen Mode</h1>

<p>
All emulators with video output include zoom level and full screen mode controls, shown below.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/computer_zoom.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Zoom Level</strong> text field</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Zoom Level</strong> spin buttons</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Full Screen</strong> button</li>
<li>(4) <strong>Terminal Zoom Level</strong> spin buttons</li>
<li>(5) <strong>Switch</strong> button</li>
<li>(6) <strong>Video Type</strong> text field</li>
</ul>

<p>
The default zoom level is 1 or 2 (depending on the emulated video type), where each dot of the emulated screen is displayed at the same size (zoom level 1) or at twice the size (zoom level 2) on the host system screen.
</p>

<p>
Set the zoom level to 0.5 or higher, depending on the host system screen size and resolution.
</p>


<h2>Zoom Level</h2>

<p>
To change the video output zoom level, use one of the following options:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Enter the desired value in the <strong>Zoom Level</strong> text field (1)</li>
<li>Use the <strong>Zoom Level</strong> spin buttons (2)</li>
<li>Drag the bottom-right corner to resize the emulated window</li>
</ul>

<p>
The zoom level for the video terminal is controlled with dedicated <strong>Terminal Zoom Level</strong> spin buttons (4) in the Terminal field. See the <a href="TerminalSetup.htm">Terminal Setup</a> section.
</p>

<h2>Full Screen Mode</h2>

<p>
To change to Full Screen Mode, use one of the following options:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Press <tt>F3</tt> in the emulated computer window</li>
<li>Use the <strong>Full Screen</strong> button (3)</li>
<li>Use the <strong>Settings/Window</strong> menu option</li>
</ul>

<p>
When both a Video Terminal and video emulation are active (e.g., on a VELF or Cosmicos), the video terminal switches to full-screen mode first. Press <tt>F3</tt> again to switch the video output to full-screen mode.
</p>

<h2>Multiple Video Outputs</h2>

<p>
If a computer configuration contains multiple video outputs, the <strong>Switch</strong> button (5) is enabled. The selected video type is shown in the <strong>Video Type</strong> text field (6). Zoom and Full Screen features apply to the currently selected video type.
</p>

<h2>Floating-Point Zooming</h2>

<p>
Floating-point zooming is enabled or disabled via <strong>Settings/Window/Enable Floating Point Zooming</strong>, shown below.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/computer_zoom_float.png" border="0" width="592" height="272">
</p>

<p>
By default, floating-point zooming is enabled, allowing more flexible use of the available window or screen space.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> Floating-point zooming increases host processor load. If screen emulation becomes too slow, disable this option.
</p>

</body>
</html>
